doc = """//! Configuration of `git-trim`.
//!
//! Every option can be given in three ways, with the following precedence:
//!
//! 1. Command line arguments (`ConfigValue::Explicit`)
//! 2. `git config` entries under the `trim` section (`ConfigValue::GitConfig`)
//! 3. Built-in defaults (`ConfigValue::Implicit`)
//!
//! # `trim.bases`
//!
//! Comma separated names of base branches. All the other branches are compared
//! with the upstream branches of those branches.
//!
//! The default value is derived from the `HEAD` of each remote:
//! `refs/remotes/<remote>/HEAD` is a symbolic reference pointing to the default
//! branch of the remote, e.g. `refs/remotes/origin/master`. Every local branch
//! that tracks such a remote tracking branch is used as a base. If no local
//! branch tracks it, the remote tracking branch itself becomes a base.
//!
//! Multiple values of `trim.bases` are allowed, and each value may itself be a
//! comma separated list. Empty elements are ignored.
//!
//! # `trim.protected`
//!
//! Comma separated glob patterns of branches that should never be deleted.
//! Patterns are matched against both the short name (`feature/foo`,
//! `origin/feature/foo`) and the full reference name (`refs/heads/feature/foo`,
//! `refs/remotes/origin/feature/foo`).
//!
//! Multiple values are allowed in the same way as `trim.bases`.
//!
//! # `trim.update`
//!
//! Whether to run `git remote update --prune` before scanning the branches.
//! Defaults to `true`. `--no-update` turns it off.
//!
